0..75 Comment "// An extension type stated by its `ext` member: `ext Cell = Val on left is"
76..148 Comment "// zero` declares the sort of cells of `Val` fixed to `zero` on the face"
149..228 Comment "// `left`, and the face theory generates its signature — `inCell` introducing"
229..307 Comment "// a cell by its values off the face, `outCellp` reading it at each point `p`,"
308..388 Comment "// and the boundary, β and η laws among the block\'s rules (Tesla Zhang, _Three"
389..461 Comment "// non-cubical applications of extension types_, arXiv:2311.05658). Each"
462..534 Comment "// generated member is named for its point by the point\'s name. Over two"
535..599 Comment "// points it is the signature `zero-fiber.gandr` writes by hand."
600..602 Comment "//"
603..617 Comment "// - see: #641"
619..695 Comment "/// The cells of `Val` over `Two` fixed to `zero` on `left`, with `c` a cell"
696..774 Comment "/// nothing introduces. The boundary reads `zero` at `left` of every cell, `c`"
775..854 Comment "/// included; β reads an introduced cell\'s value at the point off the face; η"
855..896 Comment "/// rebuilds a cell from its value there."
897..899 Other "@["
900..910 Other "normalizes"
910..911 Other "("
911..912 StringLit "\""
912..997 StringLit "cells(outCellp(c), outCellq(inCell(one)), inCell(outCellq(c))) ~> cells(zero, one, c)"
997..998 StringLit "\""
998..999 Other ")"
1000..1001 Other "]"
